    "## Raw inference latency: XGBoost vs RandomForest\n",
    "\n",
    "Measure how long the **bare fitted regressor** takes to estimate `KT10valueMax` — just feeding a\n",
    "numeric feature vector straight into the model and getting a number back, with **no** pandas\n",
    "DataFrame, `SimpleImputer`, or pipeline plumbing in the way.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each model we fit the pipeline once, pull out the fitted regressor, and feed it a plain\n",
    "`float32` numpy array. Both are trained in `log1p` space (via `TransformedTargetRegressor`), so the\n",
    "raw output is inverse-transformed with `expm1` to recover the real `KT10valueMax`. Latency is timed\n",
    "over many repeats and the **median** is reported (robust to one-off warm-up / scheduling spikes).\n",
    "\n",
    "This matters for deployment: a RandomForest must walk hundreds of full-depth trees per call, so it\n",
    "is substantially slower per prediction than a shallow boosted ensemble. If the conveyor line has a\n",
    "per-fragment time budget, check it against these numbers before picking the model.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b51ca419-f3ad-40ca-a814-cec0f5d6e962",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "from sklearn.base import clone\n",
    "\n",
    "# Single feature vector as a plain float32 numpy array (shape (1, n_features)) —\n",
    "# this is the \"just put the values in\" path, no DataFrame / imputer / pipeline overhead.\n",
    "new_sample = X.iloc[[0]].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "# RandomForest is far slower per call, so it needs fewer repeats for a stable median.\n",
    "n_repeats = {\"XGBoost\": 100_000, \"RandomForest\": 10_000}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, pipe in pipelines.items():\n",
    "    # Fit the tuned pipeline once, then pull out the bare fitted regressor.\n",
    "    inference_pipeline = clone(pipe)\n",
    "    inference_pipeline.fit(X, y)\n",
    "    model = inference_pipeline.named_steps[\"model\"].regressor_\n",
    "    model.set_params(n_jobs=1)   # single-threaded latency (lower jitter for single-row)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Warm-up call (first predict pays one-off overhead we don't want in the measurement).\n",
    "    _ = model.predict(new_sample)\n",
    "\n",
    "    repeats = n_repeats[name]\n",
    "    latencies_ms = np.empty(repeats)\n",
    "    for i in range(repeats):\n",
    "        start = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "        raw_pred = model.predict(new_sample)\n",
    "        latencies_ms[i] = (time.perf_counter() - start) * 1000.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Model was trained in log1p space -> invert to recover real KT10valueMax.\n",
    "    prediction = np.expm1(raw_pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"=== {name} ===\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Predicted KT10valueMax: {prediction[0]:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Latency over {repeats} runs (n_jobs=1):\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  median : {np.median(latencies_ms):.4f} ms\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  mean   : {latencies_ms.mean():.4f} ms\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  min    : {latencies_ms.min():.4f} ms\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  max    : {latencies_ms.max():.4f} ms\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  std    : {latencies_ms.std(ddof=1):.4f} ms\\n\")\n"
   ]
